00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
How could I ever describe this feeling? 

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
That exhilarating sense of power? That sensation that we were finally meeting our destiny. 

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
We were an army of travellers, nothing could stop us now. 

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:37.000
It was wonderful to be part of a flock, to have all eighty of us flying in the same direction, to feel we were part of something bigger, greater than ourselves. 

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:45.000
We were following the lead of the more experienced travellers, themselves following the paths of our ancestors. 

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
They took us along the Atlantic coast, a slightly longer route, but with more opportunities to rest and feed. 

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
I never thought about questioning them. It was liberating to hand over control. They had been there before, we just had to follow. 

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.000
I had a thought for the solo travellers, the scared little birds travelling alone under the cover of darkness. I pitied them. 

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.000
We didn’t have to hide, our pride carried us forward. Together, we were invincible.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:29.000
We watched human villages and roads beneath us. So small, so fragile. 

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
We remembered the poachers with their rifles, the children trying to catch us with nets and slingshots. 

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Try to catch us now, we laughed. 

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:45.000
We kept pointing excitedly at human constructions, strange things most of us had never seen before. 

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.000
A highway. A wind turbine. A power plant. 

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.000
We all cheered, when we passed them by. 

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.000
And then, suddenly our leaders grew quiet. 

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.000
I looked around, and noticed that all signs of human activity had vanished. 

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:11.000
I could feel a wave of anxiety passing among the flock: we travelled in silence, our movements tense, our necks craned. 

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.000
We knew that we were flying towards something terrible. 

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Something there were no words to describe.   

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.000
And then, we saw it.  

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Ahead of us lay an area of unimaginable emptiness. 

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
An immense stretch of land that humans had been too terrified to conquer. 

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.000
The world’s greatest desert. The Sahara. 
